option: buildable-host no
---

# platform.linux.audio

Mono signed 16-bit playback and capture through SDL2's queued audio devices.
Linux SDKs bind this provider, so generic, SDL, LCD, and other derived
Linux boards inherit the same mm.audio implementation. The audio device is
opened only when an application initializes and configures its selected Out or
In; applications that do not import mm.audio do not link SDL2 for audio.

SDL2 selects the host's audio driver and default devices. A missing playback
or capture device makes that direction's configure return TransportError.
